sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Pr as Problem
    participant Req as Requirements
    participant Math as Capacity math
    participant Arch as Architecture
    participant Fail as Failure modes
    Pr->>Req: who uses it, and what must not break?
    Req->>Req: write the SLIs and SLO targets first
    Req->>Math: peak QPS, bytes per request, retention
    Math->>Math: work per request ÷ what one machine does
    Math-->>Arch: machine count, before replication
    Arch->>Arch: draw the data flow, attach a number to every box
    Arch->>Fail: what happens when each box dies?
    Fail-->>Arch: replication factor, headroom, blast radius
    Fail->>Fail: what would page a human, and what would the runbook say?
    Note over Math,Arch: non-abstract means every component on the board has arithmetic behind it
